<title>SINGAPORE: Giken Sakata 6-months returns to profit.</title>
<headline>Giken Sakata 6-months returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     0.95	vs	(3.17)</p>
<p>    Group shares (cts)	   1.84	vs	(5.64)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     211.17	vs     132.73</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     4.28	vs	 0.42</p>
<p>    Interest expense	     0.85	vs	 0.83</p>
<p>    Depreciation		   2.51	vs	 2.79</p>
<p>Note - Electronic products manufacturer Giken Sakata Ltd said deteriorating market conditions and increasing price competition in the home audio/video industry were expected and it did not see second half results to be better than first half.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
